# HTML heads in the shapes of real READMEs

  Each part below is one head as READMEs write
  it, in words of our own. The shapes are the
  ones that read differently from a browser
  today.

                   # Harbour

        A small crate for tidal tables.

    Docs <https://example.com/docs> · Issues
          <https://example.com/issues>

  <p>

    A paragraph in a div, set apart by blank
                     lines.

  </p>

    A div whose end tag is on the line after
                another end tag.

  ▼ More

  Hidden text.

  ▼ Closed up

  Text of the details.

  A plain div in a plain div, cut by blank
  lines.

  <p>

  A plain paragraph with blank lines round its
  text.

  </p>

         A span in a centred paragraph.



